## Verified rollback backup

SSM command `ac1ca3bf-c1e1-40a0-bccc-6217f67bda7a` used SQLite's online backup API while the old service remained live. It saved database, Caddyfile, Compose file, non-exported `.env`, source revision and image ID under root-only directory:

`/opt/meatybroth-backups/pre-rust-20260913T133421Z`

Observed outcome:

- source and backup both had 8,098 posts and 33,802 follows
- backup `PRAGMA integrity_check`: `ok`
- copy-back restore-test `PRAGMA integrity_check`: `ok`; counts matched
- database SHA-256: `c9d143edfee24f84b2914f786df8e08413c66daea9b13d9d994342ee583d7811`
- size: 28 MiB

The backup is on the same root volume. It supports an in-place service rollback, not instance/volume loss. This is why the deployment must not replace the instance or delete the stack.

## Build prerequisites

Read-only package preflight found Amazon Linux packages Rust/Cargo 1.97.0. SSM command `72330950-d60e-4ddf-b89a-854f3d11c6ca` installed signed Amazon Linux `cargo`, `rust`, and `gcc` packages plus dependencies. Verified:

- `cargo 1.97.0 (Amazon Linux 1.97.0-2.amzn2023)`
- `rustc 1.97.0 (Amazon Linux 1.97.0-2.amzn2023)`
- 27 GiB remained free

No service changed. The t3.small will not compile the Rust/ONNX release.

Two off-host AL2023 link attempts established an ABI incompatibility rather than a missing compiler package. `ort-sys` rc13's prebuilt static archive references glibc ≥2.38 `__isoc23_strtol`, `__isoc23_strtoll`, `__isoc23_strtoull` and a newer libstdc++ `std::__cxx11::basic_string::_M_replace_cold`; AL2023 supplies glibc 2.34 and GCC/libstdc++ 11. Installing the correct `gcc-c++` package did not resolve it. Cached-Titan read-only runtime does not load MiniLM, but the immutable app links ONNX Runtime unconditionally.

The reviewed pivot is a pinned Ubuntu 24.04 runtime container, not an app feature change. Exact source `d1d72fc4848cb4152feb0b7115bcee3796be9da1` built off-host with the committed lockfile. Binary SHA-256: `32d12edb830f7855caa1080c7ac4348649155d7bb34bc84469eee22cce955af9`. Its only dynamic dependencies are libstdc++, libgcc_s, libm, libc and the ELF loader. The runtime base is `ubuntu:24.04@sha256:a61567bd31828687156d735ea8eb01ba4e37636e225dd6a48ba94136a70d9d61`; local image ID `sha256:f7c2ac22b5474bcf8fc752fe03305b17b8a3319365f6c9c09a0d18f60e24bbd8`, 48,175,447 bytes, numeric non-root user 10001.

A consistent 194,793,472-byte SDK snapshot passed integrity and contains 7,602 raw signed events, 149,923 social edges, planner statistics, MiniLM vectors, 119 cached Titan post vectors and six Titan topics assigning all 119 posts. The first read-only container start exposed a packaging failure: SQLite WAL mode requires a writable directory even when the main database file and application are read-only. Keeping `events.sqlite` bind-mounted read-only while mounting a 16 MiB `/data` tmpfs for WAL/SHM fixed it. The private container then returned root HTTP 200/100 cards in 0.53 s, status 200/0.08 s, cached Titan topic 200/37 cards in 0.56 s, cached Titan Similar 200/100 cards in 0.81 s, and an uncached Titan Meaning query HTTP 400 without AWS. This verifies the container method on `d1d72fc`; the final app SHA must repeat it.

